/-!
# Cubic continuity for algebraic Bernoulli convolutions

This root exposes the verified cubic development and its shared analysis,
probability, algebraic and self-similar-measure library.

The main results are `LpSelfSimilar.algebraic_bernoulli_convolution_cubic`,
its separate square-density and continuous-density conclusions,
`LpSelfSimilar.rational_bernoulli_convolution_continuous_density_cubic`, and
the natural/integer `bernoulli_convolution_one_sub_inv_continuous_density_cubic`
family. The canonical algebraic condition has exponent three and a non-strict
endpoint. The rational denominator is exactly (2+log(q)) cubed; every integer
n>=588 is covered. Density representation, nonnegativity, L2 at the squared
parameter, continuity and compact support are explicit.

`Algebraic/StrongDigitEntropy` supplies the exact finite entropy constants
3/10 and 1/2 from canonical algebraic data. Its proof uses actual Gaussian
channels, independent convolution and the contracting-conjugate matrix.
`Bernoulli/WorkingRegularityCriterion` supplies the full analytic criterion,
including L2 and strict Gaussian L1 error. Finite graph entropy, conditional
digit packing, Fourier cutoff/detail analysis, smoothing limits, Gaussian
approximation and sharp concentration stopping establish that criterion.
The `Cubic*` analysis and algebraic modules supply every quantitative input.
The existing even/odd convolution argument supplies continuity and support.

Detailed source correspondence and remaining supporting-formulation and
publication-verification obligations are recorded in the development docs.
The first-paper public statements and proofs remain unchanged.
-/
